  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are exactly 100100100 colours in the world, numbered 111 to 100100100.\n\nChef is making a 222-layered cake, and all that is left is deciding the colours of the 222 layers.\n\nChef has decided that we can choose any of the colours 1,2,…,A1, 2, \\ldots, A1,2,…,A for the first layer, and any of the colours 1,2,…,B1, 2, \\ldots, B1,2,…,B for the second layer.\n\nHowever, there is an **extra constraint**. To encourage diversity, the first and the second layer should not have the same colour.\n\nHow many different cakes are possible while following the above rules? 222 cakes are said to be different when either the first layer or the second layer has a different colour.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input contains 222 integers AAA and BBB.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput the total number of possible cakes.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤A,B≤1001 \\le A, B \\le 1001≤A,B≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2 3",
        "output": "4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe following cakes are possible: (The first number represents the colour of layer 111 and the second number the colour of layer 222)\n\n(1,2)(1, 2)(1,2)\n(1,3)(1, 3)(1,3)\n(2,1)(2, 1)(2,1)\n(2,3)(2, 3)(2,3)"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1 1",
        "output": "0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThere are no possible cakes because we must make sure layer 111 and layer 222 do not have the same colour."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "100 5",
        "output": "495",
        "explanation": ""
      }
    ]
  },
